---
import PageLayout from '../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../consts';
---

<PageLayout
  title="Terms of Use"
  description="The terms governing your use of Honest Picture — an educational, informational research library and assessment that does not provide professional advice."
  path="/terms"
  eyebrow="Trust & Legal"
  heading="Terms of Use"
  lede="Plain terms for using an educational website. By accessing or using Honest Picture, you agree to these terms."
  updated="July 2026"
>
  <h2>Acceptance of these terms</h2>
  <p>
    These Terms of Use ("Terms") govern your access to and use of
    <a href={SITE.url}>{SITE.url}</a> and its content and tools (the "site"),
    operated by {SITE.name} ("we," "us," or "our"). By accessing or using the site,
    you agree to be bound by these Terms and by our
    <a href="/privacy-policy">Privacy Policy</a> and
    <a href="/disclaimer">Disclaimer</a>. If you do not agree, please do not use the
    site.
  </p>

  <h2>Who may use the site</h2>
  <p>
    The site is intended for adults. By using it, you confirm that you are at least
    18 years old (or the age of majority where you live) and are able to enter into
    these Terms.
  </p>

  <h2>What Honest Picture is</h2>
  <p>
    {SITE.name} is an educational and informational website. It presents publicly
    available research and population data, and offers an interactive assessment
    that places your answers in that context. It is a publication and a tool — not a
    professional service, and not a substitute for professional judgment.
  </p>

  <h2>No professional advice</h2>
  <p>
    Nothing on this site is medical, psychological, financial, legal, or other
    professional advice, and nothing here creates a professional relationship. The
    assessment does not diagnose, treat, or evaluate any condition, and its output
    is context, not a recommendation. Always seek the advice of a qualified
    professional for decisions that matter, and never disregard or delay
    professional advice because of something you read here. See our full
    <a href="/disclaimer">disclaimer</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Acceptable use</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>You may read, share, and link to our pages freely for personal, non-commercial use.</li>
    <li>
      You may not scrape or harvest the site at scale, use automated systems to
      access it in a way that burdens our infrastructure, or republish substantial
      portions of our content as your own.
    </li>
    <li>
      You may not use the content to train machine-learning models or build a
      competing dataset or product without our written permission.
    </li>
    <li>
      You may not misrepresent the source or the underlying research, remove
      attributions, or present our material in a misleading way.
    </li>
    <li>
      You may not use the site for any unlawful purpose, or in any way that could
      damage, disable, overburden, or impair it or interfere with anyone else's use.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Intellectual property</h2>
  <p>
    The writing, design, structure, and original presentation on this site are owned
    by {SITE.name} and protected by intellectual-property laws. The underlying
    research and statistics belong to their respective authors and institutions,
    whom we cite. Brief quotation with clear attribution and a link back to the
    source page is welcome; anything more requires our permission.
  </p>

  <h2>Your submissions</h2>
  <p>
    If you send us feedback, corrections, or suggestions, you grant us a
    non-exclusive, royalty-free right to use them to improve the site, without
    obligation to you. Please do not send us confidential information; email
    correspondence is handled as described in our
    <a href="/privacy-policy">Privacy Policy</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Third-party links and advertising</h2>
  <p>
    The site links to third-party sources and services, and displays advertising,
    including ads served through Google AdSense. We do not control and are not
    responsible for the content, accuracy, products, or practices of third-party
    sites or advertisers, and a link or ad is not an endorsement. Your dealings with
    any third party are solely between you and that third party.
  </p>

  <h2>Accuracy and "as is"</h2>
  <p>
    We work hard to be accurate and to cite real sources, but research evolves,
    figures are rounded, and errors are possible. The site and all content are
    provided <strong>"as is" and "as available," without warranties of any kind</strong>,
    express or implied, including any implied warranties of accuracy, merchantability,
    fitness for a particular purpose, or non-infringement. We make no guarantee that
    any information is complete, current, or applicable to your specific situation,
    or that the site will be uninterrupted or error-free.
  </p>

  <h2>Limitation of liability</h2>
  <p>
    To the fullest extent permitted by law, {SITE.name} and its contributors will
    not be liable for any indirect, incidental, special, consequential, or punitive
    damages, or for any decision you make, or any loss or harm you experience, in
    connection with your use of this site or reliance on its content. Your use of the
    site is at your own discretion and risk.
  </p>

  <h2>Indemnification</h2>
  <p>
    You agree to indemnify and hold harmless {SITE.name} and its contributors from
    any claims, damages, or expenses arising out of your misuse of the site or your
    violation of these Terms.
  </p>

  <h2>Governing law</h2>
  <p>
    These Terms are governed by the laws applicable at our principal place of
    operation, without regard to conflict-of-law rules, and you agree to the
    exclusive jurisdiction of the competent courts there, except where applicable
    consumer-protection law provides otherwise.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes and severability</h2>
  <p>
    We may update these Terms over time; the "last updated" date above reflects the
    current version, and continued use of the site after changes means you accept
    them. If any provision is found unenforceable, the remaining provisions stay in
    effect.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Questions about these Terms? Email
    <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>.
  </p>
</PageLayout>
